<title>UK: Ford advert pulled after triggering epileptic fit.</title>
<headline>Ford advert pulled after triggering epileptic fit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's television advertising watchdog told Ford to withdraw a commercial for Probe cars after a viewer complained that certain scenes had triggered an epileptic seizure.</p>
<p>The Ford advertisement broke technical guidelines designed to prevent bright lights from triggering attacks in viewers who suffer &quot;photo-sensitive epilspy&quot;, said the Independent Television Commission.</p>
<p>The ITC ordered Ford to discontinue the commercial, devised by  British firm Ogilvy &amp; Mather. It said the commercial was subsequently changed.</p>
</text>
